{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1458672-sensing-shapeshifters","id":1458672,"title":"Sensing Shapeshifters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-04T07:13:38-07:00","id":1458672,"title":"Sensing Shapeshifters","content":"Hi!<br /> <br /> My players are at war with some Shapeshifters and want to do a ritual to sense all the shapeshifters they can in a small city (100.000 inhabitants). I guess that would be Spirit plus Life and Correspondence, but what levels? How many successes would they need? <br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T11:58:57-07:00","id":1458703,"title":"","content":"Correspondence 2, rest 1. Spheres wise this is just perception, the most basic magic.<br /> <br /> For the area, a shitton of successes:<br /> +1 for affecting someone else;<br /> +5 in Range 'cause no way they visited every cranny of the city to be lower than that;<br /> +1 in duration to have at least a scene to analyze the info;<br /> +5 in Gauntlet to seek Shapeshifters in the local Penumbra;<br /> +X where X is every Shapeshifter in town to be localized.<br /> <br /> So best case scenario it is still 13 successes (or 12 and there's no Shapeshifters in town). Put there a pack of four, and it is 16 successes. A Caern with 10 members wandering about and it goes all the way up to 22. And the players can't even know for sure how many successes they need, so they have to establish a target and go for it, if it is not enough, scrap it and start again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T12:27:34-07:00","id":1458707,"title":"","content":"First off, for clarity, when you say shapeshifters, do you mean the ones detailed in the WtA books? It seems so if we're talking Life/Spirit, but there's plenty of other things that count as shapeshifters in the WoD that aren't that.<br /> <br /> On what you need for detection, it somewhat depends on what level of certainty you want. Technically Mind 1 or Spirit1 (or Prime 1 in some editions) alone can work, because they can let you examine auras, and the werecritters have distinct auras, but there's a high degree of risk of missing some. Generally speaking, you're not going to need more than 1 dot Spheres here to be more certain, but the more you toss in the harder it will be for edge cases to slip by you. Life 1/Mind 1/Prime 1/Spirit 1 is probably the limit of being completely thorough in this regard for a particularly paranoid mage.<br /> <br /> On the matter of scale, Correspondence 3 is when you get to scanning large areas like this. By itself that's all you need for a city. But if we're talking werecritters, the snag is going to come into if you want to scan into the Umbra as well. That's going to tack on Spirit 3 at a minimum, and you could make a case for bumping that up to Correspondence 4 to scan two different realms of existence at the same time.<br /> <br /> On the number of successes? Again, there's a level of how certain do they want to be. One of the larger practical limitations on Correspondence is familiarity/sympathy (in a mystic sense). Scanning for someone you've never even heard of, and have no bridge to (such as an object that person holds a deep emotional connection to), is a lot of successes to overcome. But basically this should come into the Outlandish Feat range (10 to 20 successes), but this falls under ST discretion as you're getting to the &quot;however difficult the ST wants this to be&quot; part of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T13:01:35-07:00","id":1458711,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> \u200bI don't think Spirit or Correspondence need to be particularly high. Spirit 1 is enough to peak to the Penumbra, and this effect doesn't need more than that. Correspondence 2 is enough to sense through distance, again the limit of what this effects strives to achieve. There are benefits in having higher levels, but the bare minimum is there, by M20 rules.<br /> <br /> The number of successes is trickier, but above I outlined the most objective (not necessarily better or more correct) way to get it. There are several ways of looking at this problem, but in the end it is a question of successes, not spheres. I totally agree that adding spheres to the effect will help a lot. The perfect set would have Life, Spirit, Mind, Prime and Correspondence, maybe Entropy if they want to find out children that will Change in the future.<br /> <br /> More importantly, it requires a firm grasp of what is it that they're looking for. That's why I only referred to Shapechangers in my answer, because this is a broad category that may include a lot of things. And the <u>characters <b>have to</b></u> understand those things if they want to look for them. If they have a poor conceptual grasp of what they're looking for, a perfect spell will still get a lot of noise, loss a lot of targets, or both. And still be hard as Hell to execute.<br /> <br /> In the end this is simple Spheres wise, but heavy in scope. Without narrowing a little the search they're going for anything but easy solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T15:07:14-07:00","id":1458734,"title":"","content":"There's always a level of interpretation here. <br /> <br /> I wouldn't call scouring the local Penumbra for every shifter there &quot;peeking&quot; thus needing to actually pierce the Gauntlet with Spirit 3 to thoroughly search it. Even then, peeking requires an appropriate Vidare for the part of the Umbra you're attuned to, so plenty of mages aren't on the right wavelength to peek for shifters (and of course, Shifters might natively be on the Spiritus wavelength, but they can get to states appropriate to Astral or Mortem with the right tricks). Less interpretation, you need Correspondence 3 to sense multiple locations at the same time. Correspondence 2 only lets you send your perceptions to one other place. I guess, in theory, you could get away with Correspondence 2 and one success per additioanl target location, but in a city of the size in question that would skyrocket the requisite successes to a ridiculous degree (to put this in perspective, the closest city to me is less than 100K people, and if you required 1 success per city block, that would be ~900 successes from that alone).<br /> <br /> As for the number of successes... I'm not really sure where you're getting some of your numbers. There's not requirement for you to extend an effect's duration in order to think about what you saw, and the whole point of doing an area of effect style spell is so you don't have to spend successes on every potential target like that. If I use Forces to set fire to a building, I don't need to spend a success for every potential victim of the blaze, and if I use Correspondence to see around a corner I don't need to spend successes for every person I can see that I couldn't see before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T18:20:27-07:00","id":1458755,"title":"","content":"You're right that there's a level of interpretation, so I'll just add some more of my thoughts. Argonot is the final arbiter of what will happens, anyway.<br /> <br /> I'm usually in favor of letting added Spheres facilitate things, and most of the work is being done by other Spheres than Spirit, which is mostly confirming if the Pattern found pings for spirit with a few qualities. It could be argued that Spirit 2 is necessary to move the effect into the Umbra, but Spirit 3, when used to read information on spirits, is so thorough that I think it would be enough to identify a Shapeshifter by itself, without Life.<br /> <br /> Correspondence 2 was based in the least level needed to pull out the effect, and is the reason to give it a duration. The effect extends perception to the entire city, but since you can't sense multiple locations you need time to digest the information properly. Otherwise a higher level of Mind could be required. I do agree that Correspondence 3 would be better, though.<br /> <br /> My use of targets was a haphazardly way to compensate that I didn't found any factor for area in the charts and it accounted for your suggestion of +1 success per area, but I'm actually quite unhappy with it, you're right. Going with my idea of maximum variety of Spheres, but at the lowest levels possible, I think I would change it for an &quot;Area factor&quot; of 4 or 5 successes. As in other factors, I think this Area one should have an exponential progression, not a linear one.<br /> <br /> The truth of the matter, though, is that this effect can be done in several different ways, we diverged in assumptions more than in actual interpretations (although there is a divergence). Adding levels in certain Spheres can help this effect in many ways. The best possible situation would be Correspondence 3, Life 1, Mind 2, Prime 1 and Spirit 3. But even then, the sheer scope of the feat would make it at the very least 12 successes.<br /> <br /> Limiting this insane scope will reduce the number of successes dramatically. A big part of the problem is that &quot;reading the entire city&quot; means reading a lot of places the characters barely know are there and dealing with all the thick Gauntlet areas. Depending on interpretations on those things it would be reasonable to add even more required successes, I went relatively low on the premise that a map of the city is at hand and nowhere the Gauntlet will be effectively protected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T09:12:08-07:00","id":1459441,"title":"","content":"Guys, this discussion has been extremely useful. Thank you very much for taking the time to participate. <br /> <br /> I actually think Correspondence 3 would be better to pull out the effect in a broader form (as described).<br /> <br /> The player who can do the sensing ritual only has 2 points in Correspondence. But he developed a way to create &quot;connections&quot; with places through some flowers he grows and bathes using his own blood. I will tell him that it is easier to distribute those flowers around to use them as &quot;anchor points&quot; for his senses, effectively dividing the city in &quot;sectors&quot;. He can cast a sensing ritual for each sector, supposing he can keep up with the physical and mental effort. <br /> <br /> Besides, requiring Corr 3 (Co-Locality Perception...and MInd, probably) to sense two realms at a time sounds about right, so he would be confined to Earth or Umbra...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T09:37:37-07:00","id":1459444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1458672-sensing-shapeshifters?p=1459441#post1459441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, requiring Corr 3 (Co-Locality Perception...and MInd, probably) to sense two realms at a time sounds about right, so he would be confined to Earth or Umbra...</div> </div> </div> </div>Co-location isn't to look into two realms, Spirit does that. What it makes is for the Mage to perceive the entire city at once. Without Correspondence 3 he will be limited to look at a single flower at each casting.<br /> <br /> The flowers are a really good way to reduce the successes needed, but will let a lot of blind spots in this effect. As a rule of thumb, even with Correspondence 3 the flower will help only to observe within line of sight of the flower itself, not the entire block or even entire building. Getting those flowers in position is also something to be worked, otherwise just giving them out won't get them really all over the place.<br /> <br /> But accepting this limitation could really help things out. If your player accepts to just look from one flower at a time and be limited by line of sight (getting to look at the Umbra, too, with enough Spirit), this should be just 2 success per casting, which is absolutely doable, repeatable, and the flowers can be used as long as they last for other effects.<br /> <br /> Otherwise you can't really circumvent this without ignoring the rules, though. If you personally want, as the ST, to let them scan the entire city, go ahead. But by RAW this is a feat for at least 10 successes no matter what Sphere combination you get. This is simply too huge an achievement otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}